>Say I am a lawful Character and I kill a neutral unicorn, the alter
>next to me is also neutral, should I offer it, or should I convert
>the alter to my allignment first.

>in other words, I should be co-alligned with the alter I am offering
>the non-co-alligned unicorn on. The unicorn doesn't have to
>be co-alligned with the alter that I am offering it on. correct ?

Do NOT #offer a X-aligned unicorn on a X-aligned altar, regardless of
your alingment.  If the unicorn is neutral, the altar is neutral,
and you are something else (and you want to stay that alignment),
then #offer something else on that altar (converting it), and THEN
#offer the unicorn to give your alingment score a big boost.

I once made the mistake of #offering a L unicorn at a L altar, when
I was neutral thinking (whew boy, Ill definately convert the altar
with this sacrifice!  My N god will love me!).  What happened instead
was I got some really ominous nastry message about what a sacrilige I
did and how pissed off the L god was.  I dont know what effect the
act had on my alignment, but it didnt convert the altar.

